{"step_index":765,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T00:01:29Z","thinking":"**Quantifying Information Discrepancies.**\n\nSignificant data discrepancies detected between user-provided data and the fact-checked dataset. The user's input contains 211 phone numbers absent in the fact-checked data. The fact-checked dataset, in turn, includes substantial numbers of missing zip codes, addresses, employee counts, and corporate numbers. This highlights a need to understand the implications of these differences.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Data for Merge.**\n\nThe user's input likely represents the most up-to-date data, requiring careful preservation during merging with the fact-checked dataset. Blind overwriting risks losing critical user-provided information, particularly phone numbers. A strategy to create a master dataset that incorporates user preferences and combines facts from the verified source is needed. This will be done by prioritizing and preserving user data in several columns, such as phone numbers, while filling in gaps with the fact-checked data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e \"\nconst fs = require('fs');\n\nconst pastedRaw = fs.readFileSync('current_pasted_batch.tsv', 'utf-8');\nconst pastedLines = pastedRaw.split('\\n').map(l => l.trim()).filter(l => l.startsWith('배현명'));\n\nconst factRaw = fs.readFileSync('all_500_factchecked.tsv', 'utf-8');\nconst factLines = factRaw.split('\\n').map(l => l.trim()).filter(l => l.length > 0);\n\nconsole.log('Merging 500 rows...');\nconst mergedRows = [];\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < 500; i++) {\n  const p = pastedLines[i].split('\\t');\n  const f = factLines[i].split('\\t');\n  \n  // Columns:\n  // 0: author\n  const author = '배현명';\n  \n  // 1: remark (폐업, 휴업)\n  const remark = (p[1] && p[1].trim()) ? p[1].trim() : (f[1] && f[1].trim() ? f[1].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 2: company\n  const company = (p[2] && p[2].trim()) ? p[2].trim() : f[2].trim();\n  \n  // 3: bizno\n  const bizno = p[3].trim();\n  \n  // 4: ceo\n  const ceo = (p[4] && p[4].trim()) ? p[4].trim() : (f[4] && f[4].trim() ? f[4].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 5: zip (5 digits)\n  let zip = (p[5] && p[5].trim() && /^[0-9]{5}$/.test(p[5].trim())) ? p[5].trim() : (f[5] && f[5].trim() ? f[5].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 6: address\n  let addr = (p[6] && p[6].trim().length > 5) ? p[6].trim() : (f[6] && f[6].trim() ? f[6].trim() : '');\n  // if p[6] has only province/city (short like '경상남도 양산시'), prefer f[6]\n  if (p[6] && p[6].trim().length < 15 && f[6] && f[6].trim().length > 15) {\n    addr = f[6].trim();\n  }\n  \n  // 7: tel\n  let tel = (p[7] && p[7].trim() && p[7].trim() !== '-' && p[7].trim() !== '--') ? p[7].trim() : (f[7] && f[7].trim() && f[7].trim() !== '--' && f[7].trim() !== '-' ? f[7].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 8: fax\n  let fax = (p[8] && p[8].trim() && p[8].trim() !== '-' && p[8].trim() !== '--') ? p[8].trim() : (f[8] && f[8].trim() && f[8].trim() !== '--' && f[8].trim() !== '-' ? f[8].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 9: homepage\n  let homepage = (p[9] && p[9].trim() && p[9].startsWith('http')) ? p[9].trim() : (f[9] && f[9].trim() && f[9].startsWith('http') ? f[9].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 10: email\n  let email = (p[10] && p[10].trim() && p[10].includes('@')) ? p[10].trim() : (f[10] && f[10].trim() && f[10].includes('@') ? f[10].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 11: emp count\n  let emp = (p[11] && p[11].trim() && p[11].trim() !== '0') ? p[11].trim() : (f[11] && f[11].trim() ? f[11].trim() : (p[11] ? p[11].trim() : ''));\n  // clean '명' or '20미만'\n  emp = emp.replace('명', '').trim();\n  \n  // 12: nice industry\n  let nice = (f[12] && f[12].trim()) ? f[12].trim() : (p[12] && p[12].trim() ? p[12].trim() : '');\n  \n  // 13: corpNo (13 digits with hyphen)\n  let corpNo = (p[13] && p[13].trim() && p[13].trim().replace(/[^0-9]/g, '').length === 13) ? p[13].trim() : (f[13] && f[13].trim() ? f[13].trim() : '');\n  if (corpNo && /^[0-9]{13}$/.test(corpNo)) {\n    corpNo = corpNo.substring(0, 6) + '-' + corpNo.substring(6);\n  }\n  \n  // 14: settlement month\n  let settle = (p[14] && p[14].trim()) ? p[14].trim() : (f[14] && f[14].trim() ? f[14].trim() : (corpNo ? '12월' : ''));\n  \n  // 15, 16, 17: categories\n  let catL = (f[15] && f[15].trim()) ? f[15].trim() : (p[15] && p[15].trim() ? p[15].trim() : '');\n  let catM = (f[16] && f[16].trim()) ? f[16].trim() : (p[16] && p[16].trim() ? p[16].trim() : '');\n  let catS = (f[17] && f[17].trim()) ? f[17].trim() : (p[17] && p[17].trim() ? p[17].trim() : '');\n  \n  mergedRows.push([\n    author, remark, company, bizno, ceo, zip, addr, tel, fax, homepage, email, emp, nice, corpNo, settle, catL, catM, catS\n  ].join('\\t'));\n}\n\nfs.writeFileSync('merged_500_perfect.tsv', mergedRows.join('\\n'), 'utf-8');\nconsole.log('Successfully generated merged_500_perfect.tsv with 500 rows!');\n\"","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\lg\\resilient-bardeen","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Generating merged 500 perfect rows","toolSummary":"Generate merged_500_perfect.tsv"}}]}
